Cursor has no direct SKILL.md equivalent (no on-demand invocation, only always-on or
glob-scoped rules), so this file plays the same role as
`.claude/skills/scaffold-endpoint/SKILL.md` — same content, reference that file for the
full reference-example code blocks if this one is trimmed for length.

When asked to add a new REST endpoint to `apps/api`, build bottom-up:

1. Shared Zod schema in `packages/shared/src/<resource>.ts` (skip if it already exists
   — check `book.ts`/`review.ts`/`shelf.ts` first), re-exported from `index.ts`.
2. Repository function in `apps/api/src/data/<resource>.repository.ts` — writes go
   through `mutateCollection()`, ids are `<prefix>_NNN` generated inside the mutator.
3. Service function in `apps/api/src/services/<resource>.service.ts` — no `req`/`res`,
   builds records field-by-field, throws typed errors from `../errors`.
4. Route handler — nest sub-resources on the parent router (e.g. reviews go on
   `booksRouter` as `/:id/reviews`); no `try/catch`, no `asyncHandler`.
5. Wire a new top-level router into `routes/index.ts` if it isn't a sub-resource.
6. `node:test` file in `apps/api/tests/` mirroring `books.test.ts`'s isolated-temp-dir
   + dynamic-`import('../src/app')` pattern.

Constraints: static routes (`/search`) before `/:id` at the same depth; response
envelope is `{ data }` / `{ error: { code, message, details? } }`; `POST` → 201 +
`Location`; `DELETE` → 204 or 404; never spread raw input into a repository call;
never add a dependency without asking.
